      },
      "cites": ["P1.3"]
    },
    {
      "id": "n3",
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Key Granularity and Limitations",
      "content": {
        "markdown": "Keys can be defined with varying levels of granularity. However, each key adds to the header length, and systems like Larkspur impose a limit (e.g., under 50 keys per response) to prevent excessive header size."
